+// The marks (PPFileData.marks) of tokens [begin, end), a word per 64 from `begin`, a multiple of 64: '#' and '##' by
+// their kinds, and __VA_OPT__ on a directive's line by an identifier's id, its value (another token's value is its end,
+// which may equal the id). The ids are read only for the 64 tokens that hold a directive's line: one with a directive's
+// '#' (a line's first token), or one that starts within the line of the last's. `*directive` says whether the tokens
+// before `begin` end on a directive's line, and is left saying it of those before `end`.
+static void pp_mark_tokens(const uint8_t* kinds, const uint32_t* values, uint32_t begin, uint32_t end, uint64_t* marks, bool* directive)
+{
+    bool open = *directive;
+    for (uint32_t i = begin; i < end; i += 64)
